# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Created package.json
- Initialized npm package configuration with `npm init -y`
- This enables dependency management for the project

### 2. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 as a dependency
- Created package-lock.json to lock dependency versions

### 3. Modified index.html
- Added Vercel Web Analytics script in the `<head>` section
- Implemented vanilla JavaScript integration as per official Vercel documentation:
  - Added initialization script with `window.va` function
  - Added deferred script tag loading from `/_vercel/insights/script.js`

### Files Modified
- `index.html` - Added analytics initialization scripts
- `package.json` - Created with @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Created to lock dependency versions

## Implementation Details

The analytics implementation follows Vercel's official quickstart guide for vanilla JavaScript projects:
- Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Used the recommended vanilla JavaScript integration pattern
- Scripts are placed in the HTML head for optimal loading
- The defer attribute ensures non-blocking script execution

## How It Works

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The `/_vercel/insights/script.js` endpoint will be automatically available
2. Analytics will track page views and user interactions
3. Data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
4. No additional configuration is required - it works out of the box

## Next Steps for Deployment

1. Enable Analytics in your Vercel project dashboard
2. Deploy the project using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify analytics are working by checking the Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`
4. View analytics data in your Vercel dashboard

## Notes
- The implementation preserves all existing functionality
- No breaking changes to the codebase
- Analytics script loads asynchronously to avoid impacting page performance
- Compatible with all modern browsers
